![Slide image 8](assets/lect02c-genome_sizes/image_008.png)

@right

- Most known chromosomes
- Adders-tongue
- Ophioglossum reticulatum
- Fern with a stalk is thought to resemble a snake's tongue
- Has about 1260 chromosomes in its diploid cells

=== layout: section

# Total DNA mass

=== layout: two-panels

# First Genome in 1995

@left

- The first free-living organism to have its genome completely sequenced was the bacterium Haemophilus influenzae, in 1995.
  - A non-moving rod-shaped bacterium that causes meningitis.
  - Genome size of 1.8 million base pairs

@right

![Slide image 9](assets/lect02c-genome_sizes/image_009.png)

