=== layout: two-panels

# Human Genome Project

@left

- One of the most interesting projects in modern genetics was the sequencing of the entire human genome
  - A genome is the complete set of genes (and alleles) in a certain organism
- The Human Genome Project, begun in 1989 and essentially finished in 2003, was a massive research undertaking

@right

![Slide image 13](assets/lect02c-genome_sizes/image_013.png)

=== layout: two-panels

# Genome Sequence History

@left

- 1976 – Phage MS2 – 3.5 kbp
- 1995 – H. influenza – 1.8 Mbp
- 1996 – S. cerevisiae – 12.1 Mbp
- 1998 – C. elegans – 100 Mbp
- 2000 – Arabidopsis – 119 Mbp
- 2000 – Drosophila – 165 Mbp
- 2003 – Human – 3.2 Gbp
- 2005 – Rice – 430 Mbp
- 2009 – Corn – 2.3 Gbp
- 2014 – Pine tree – 21 Gbp
  - 82% duplicated
- TBD – Japanese canopy plant – 150 Gbp

@right

![Slide image 14](assets/lect02c-genome_sizes/image_014.png)

