=== layout: two-plus-one-panels

# SNP rs2802292

@top-left

- A study of 5 genes in 3,741 Japanese men
  - some of whom lived significantly longer than average (centarians)
- concluded that the FOXO3 gene harbors several SNPs linked to longevity, including this SNP, rs2802292
  - as well as rs2764264 and rs13217795.

@bottom-left

- [https\://www.snpedia.com/index.php/Rs2802292](https://www.snpedia.com/index.php/Rs2802292)

@right

![Slide image 25](assets/lect02c-genome_sizes/image_025.png)

- 23andMe for
- Dr. Voss\: G;T

=== layout: two-panels

# Promethease

@left

- Promethease is a literature retrieval system that builds a personal DNA report based on connecting a file of DNA genotypes to the scientific findings cited in SNPedia.
  - Customers of DNA testing services (such as 23andMe, Ancestry.com, FamilyTreeDNA, etc.), can retrieve information published science articles about their DNA variations.

@right

![Slide image 26](assets/lect02c-genome_sizes/image_026.png)

=== layout: section

# Number of Genes

=== layout: two-over-one-panels

# Minimal Organism

@top-left

- Mycoplasma laboratorium is a designed, partially synthetic species of bacterium
  - It is estimated that the synthetic genome cost US\$40 million to make and took 20 people more than a decade of work.
- Version 3.0 – contains 531,560 base pairs and 473 genes.
  - Of these genes 149 are of unknown biological function.
  - announced March 24, 2016

@top-right

![Slide image 27](assets/lect02c-genome_sizes/image_027.png)

@bottom

- [http\://astrobiology.com/2016/03/first-minimal-synthetic-bacterial-cell.html](http://astrobiology.com/2016/03/first-minimal-synthetic-bacterial-cell.html)

- [https\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mycoplasma\_laboratorium](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mycoplasma_laboratorium)

